/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/_logs/4.log:3150:#      of that older beam must be recolored from the crossing onward.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/_logs/4.log:3152:#    - Pure color exchange is easy to miss if many same-color beams interact, so the generator gives
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/_logs/4.log:3159:#    - Any code that truncates beams, blocks cells permanently, or rewrites direction on collision must
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/_logs/4.log:3160:#      be removed. Instead we need persistent per-beam paths so a late crossing can recolor an already
