/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/_logs/4.log:3167:#    - Candidate corner gaps are filtered so each beam has at least a short unobstructed diagonal runway.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/_logs/4.log:3173:#    - Restricting to corner gaps avoids hidden bookkeeping with cardinal beams whose collisions would
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/_logs/4.log:3176:#    - One beam per frame and diagonal-only motion keep the grids readable.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/_logs/4.log:3180:#    - Every beam color comes from a unique source block, so when two continuations exchange colors the
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/_logs/4.log:3182:#    - There is no hidden dependence on color ids; only visible beam/block correspondences matter.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/_logs/4.log:3184:#    - All legal variant inputs use corner gaps only, so every beam is diagonal.
